cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fp_analysis: An interactive desktop application for perievent analysis of fiber photometry recordings"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yue
    family-names: Zhao
    affiliation: "University of Rochester, Rochester, NY, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-5012"
abstract: >-
  An open-source desktop application for visualizing and analyzing fiber
  photometry recordings. The app loads MATLAB .mat recordings containing up to
  four photometry signal channels, presents them as synchronized interactive
  traces that can be zoomed and navigated independently along either axis, and
  aligns them to a list of events supplied as a spreadsheet in either a
  transition-table or an event-table layout. For a chosen event type and a
  chosen pair of baseline and analysis windows, it computes and plots the raw
  and baseline-normalized perievent traces, their mean, and a per-occurrence
  heatmap, together with summary metrics: area under the curve, positive and
  negative peak values, time to first peak, and decay time. When two signals
  are selected it also computes their mean normalized cross-correlation.
  Results are exported to spreadsheet workbooks that are grouped by analysis
  setup, so repeated exports accumulate subjects side by side rather than
  duplicating them. The packaged Windows build runs without a Python
  installation or an internet connection and checks GitHub Releases for
  compatible source updates at startup.
repository-code: "https://github.com/yzhaoinuw/fp_analysis"
license: MIT
version: 0.6.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
keywords:
  - fiber photometry
  - photometry
  - neuroscience
  - perievent analysis
  - time series
  - desktop application
  - research software
